\f5\i \cf0 Why were men such bloody whiners? They did naught but whinge, bitch and complain. 
\f4\i0 Now alone, Sarah immediately went to work, but merely reversing her previous key strokes had no effect, after a bit of trial and error she finally managed direct the water back into the recyc system. She received no congratulations from the engineers though. \
\'93She was just lucky\'94 they all decided and promptly left nursing battered egos. \'93This is a disgrace, Lieutenant, who are these people?\'94\
\'93Don\'92t worry, I won\'92t mention them in my report. I will give you all the credit. Okay?\'94\
\'93Yes. That seems acceptable,\'94 said a senior engineer. 
\f5\i Fixing this will look good on my resume.
\f4\i0 \
The choked drain had caused a cascade of brown water spill out the entrance and flood the basement, all three levels and then out into the street. Blue prints of the building proved entirely inaccurate, causing the city workers to wade around hopelessly in a fruitless search for the blockage. Cracker, hooked on a life line and waded in, heading straight for the logjam. The water was chest deep and he had to duck-dive to unblock it. He dragged and jerked at the main chunks of flotsam and finally heaved up the bloated corpse of a communist lard-arse. His reign of socialist terror lasting long enough for him to slip and wedge his enormous behind in the drain.\
\'93Here\'92s your terrorist, Shakti.\'94 Cracker proudly announced as he floated the body to the stair. After a few more diving missions, the drain was unclogged and sucking water down greedily. \'93You\'92re a hero now, mate. The rest is just a simple mop and squeegee job, other contractors can take care of it.\'94\
\'93I\'92ll have one of my minions take you both home. Neither of you were here. Understand?\'94 Now that the crisis was over, he did not want these two hanging around to take the limelight. He had a boss to impress.
